  "question": "A playlist mixes 10 artists equally and shuffles truly at random. How soon do two songs by one artist play back to back?",
  "answer": "Within a handful of songs. Each song has a one-in-ten chance of matching the artist before it, and the chances pile up: past eight songs a pair is more likely than not. Spotify changed its shuffle in 2014 to spread artists out: less random, so it felt more random.",
  "move": "Expect chance to clump; evenly spread results are the suspicious ones.",
  "ask": "Which streak of bad luck in my life did I read as a pattern when it was just chance clumping?",
